WasmFS sockets, epoll, eventfd, socketpair and blocking poll, for OpenJDK's libnet/libnio (Socket, SocketChannel,
Selector, Netty NIO) running under IKVM in ikvmcraft. WasmFS returned ENOSYS for every socket syscall and for epoll,
its poll() never blocked, an empty pipe read as EOF while a writer was alive, dup2() over an open descriptor never
closed the file it replaced, and libc had no eventfd. Now:
- Pipes, sockets, eventfds and epoll instances are stream files (system/lib/wasmfs/stream_file.h; the lock order is
  documented there). read/write/send/recv/poll/epoll_wait/connect run without the File and OpenFileState locks and
  block on a futex until the file notifies, a timeout passes, close() of the last descriptor (EBADF), or a signal:
  pthread_kill() now also wakes a target blocked in emscripten_futex_wait (pthread_kill.c), the blocked syscall runs
  the thread's system queue, and returns EINTR if a handler ran (raise.c counts them; read/write/connect only count
  handlers without SA_RESTART). O_NONBLOCK (fcntl, FIONBIO, pipe2, SOCK_NONBLOCK, EFD_NONBLOCK) gives EAGAIN. The
  main browser thread never blocks: there every descriptor acts non-blocking and timeouts are zero.
- poll()/select() block; an empty pipe with a live writer is EAGAIN or blocks; dup2/dup3 closes what it replaces.
- epoll with emscripten #27207's semantics (LT/ET/ONESHOT/EXCLUSIVE/RDHUP, nesting and ELOOP, dup sharing,
  round-robin past maxevents, eviction when the watched description closes; zero timeouts go through
  __syscall_epoll_pwait_nonblocking as in #27207). eventfd: musl's eventfd.c, <sys/eventfd.h>, SYS_eventfd2.
- socketpair(AF_UNIX, SOCK_STREAM). AF_INET/AF_INET6 TCP client sockets over a transport the embedder supplies
  (src/lib/libwasmfs_sockets.js documents it: globalThis.wasmfsSocketTransport = {connect, send, shutdown?, close,
  pause?, resume?}, installed with --pre-js so it exists in every worker; none installed: ENETUNREACH), owned by one
  dedicated network pthread that syscalls post to and never wait on. Sends are bounded by SO_SNDBUF until the
  transport reports them drained. listen/accept are EOPNOTSUPP, UDP sends ENETUNREACH, there is no SIGPIPE.
- getaddrinfo/getnameinfo/gethostbyname resolve in C (resolver.cpp) to fake 240.67.0.0/16 addresses that connect()
  maps back to the hostname for the transport, replacing libcore.js's JS versions (which proxy to the main thread).
Applies after emsdk.11.patch. Rebuild: embuilder build --force sysroot (new header) libc* libwasmfs*
libstandalonewasm*. Tests (test/wasmfs/wasmfs_*.c, the loopback transport wasmfs_sockets_transport.js, and
test_other.py's test_wasmfs_*) are on the source branch only: .NET's emsdk has no test/.

From emscripten-6.0.2 branch wasmfs-sockets (5b11e23 5adfe1d 36cd282 e17bc8b ) on fna-dotnet (.NET's emscripten 6.0.3 6ea9c28c38cd + emsdk.3-11).

